\ Cross-module visibility for protocol-bounded parameters. Runs under
\ `1z check`; `type-check: "warning"` keeps the run alive while making
\ analyzer diagnostics observable on stderr.
\
\ The protocol `xmod-scaleable` has a single cross-type method
\ (`xmod-scale: ( a: self b: any -- result )`) whose registration for
\ `xmod-widget` lives in `proto_xmod_methods.1z`. The analyzer must
\ stay silent at the call site whether or not the methods module has
\ loaded, since the runtime check covers the cross-type path.
pragma{ type-check: "warning" }

use "fixtures/proto_xmod_protocol.1z" ;
use "fixtures/proto_xmod_type.1z" ;

\ Producer yields the virtual type without any method registration.
make-widget: ( -- y: xmod-widget ) [ 5 >xmod-widget ] ;

\ Consumer accepts the protocol-bound parameter.
consume-scaleable: ( x: xmod-scaleable -- ) [ drop ] ;

\ Pipeline before the methods module loads. Even though no
\ `xmod-scale: method{ xmod-widget any }` is registered yet, the
\ analyzer must not emit a diagnostic because the protocol's only
\ requirement is cross-type.
unloaded-pipeline: ( -- ) [ make-widget consume-scaleable ] ;

\ Load the contributing methods module and confirm the same composition
\ stays silent.
use "fixtures/proto_xmod_methods.1z" ;

loaded-pipeline: ( -- ) [ make-widget consume-scaleable ] ;
